/*!
  \page example_sycl_kdtree_page Using kd-trees in SYCL kernels

  This example is the SYCL counterpart of \ref example_cu_kdtree_page. A kd-tree is built on the CPU, its buffers are
  copied to device memory with SYCL allocations (helper functions of `examples/sycl/sycl_kdtree.h`), and the kernel
  queries the tree to collect the neighbors of each point before fitting a plane.

  The example is compiled when <a href="https://adaptivecpp.github.io/" target="_blank">AdaptiveCpp</a> is found by
  CMake:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_fit_kdtree_sycl
  ./build/examples/sycl/ponca_fit_kdtree_sycl
  \endcode

  See also \ref ponca_gpu_sycl.

  \include sycl/ponca_fit_kdtree.cpp
*/
